---
/**
 * FAQs - DESIGN.md 14.6. Copy from COPY.md, "FAQs", verbatim.
 *
 * The quietest masthead on the site, then one Accordion (7.6) holding all
 * three question groups so the strap-draw divider between groups is the
 * only rule doing the separating - three separate <Accordion>s would each
 * add their own plain top hairline on top of it.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Accordion from '../components/Accordion.astro';
import AccordionItem from '../components/AccordionItem.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
import Media from '../components/Media.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';

import { site, labels } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="FAQs - Islamic School of Potomac"
  description="Ages, tuition, placement, what a Sunday looks like, and how to get involved. The questions families ask us most."
>
  {/* 1. Masthead */}
  <Masthead preset="faqs" label="QUESTIONS" lines={['What families', 'ask us.']} />

  {/* 2. The list */}
  <Section ground="paper" container="narrow" rhythm="sm">
    <Accordion>
      <h2 class="t-label faq-group">ENROLLING</h2>

      <AccordionItem question="How old does my child need to be?" id="faq-age" open>
        <p class="t-body">
          Our classes begin at kindergarten, with 5 year-olds. The school teaches children through
          age 18.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question="How much does it cost?" id="faq-cost">
        <p class="t-body">
          The cost is $60 for one student and $100 for a family. Financial assistance is
          available.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question="What if tuition is a difficulty for us?" id="faq-tuition">
        <p class="t-body">
          Financial assistance is available and it is handled quietly. It is a normal part of how
          this school works, not an exception to it.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question="How are children placed in classes?" id="faq-placement">
        <p class="t-body">
          Arabic class placement is determined by placement test. Deen class placement is
          determined by the age of the student.
        </p>
        <p class="t-body">
          The Arabic test is short, it happens on the first day of school, and nobody passes or
          fails it. It exists so a child sits with others reading at the same level rather than
          others born the same year.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question="How do I enroll?" id="faq-how-to-enroll">
        <p class="t-body">
          Through the enrollment form on this site. It takes a few minutes, and someone from the
          school will write back about placement.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <Divider />
      <h2 class="t-label faq-group">THE PROGRAM</h2>

      <AccordionItem question="What is the Noorani method?" id="faq-noorani">
        <p class="t-body">
          A well-established approach to teaching Arabic recitation, which builds up from letters
          and their sounds to reading whole words and verses. It is what we use to teach children
          to read the Quran.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question="What does Deen class cover?" id="faq-deen">
        <p class="t-body">
          Deen is taught thematically rather than from a fixed textbook. The school takes a theme
          and every grade works on it in a way that suits its age, so a family with children of
          different ages is having one conversation at home rather than several.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question={'What is "...and in between"?'} id="faq-between">
        <p class="t-body">
          The school's name for everything that happens outside class: the friendships, the
          questions asked in hallways, the habit of showing up.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question="Do you give homework?" id="faq-homework">
        <p class="t-body">
          Children have enough homework during the week. We don't give homework to children - we
          give it to the parents!
        </p>
        <p class="t-body">
          In practice: the school asks families to reinforce what is taught by doing it together.
          Praying, giving, serving the community. A child who is told about charity learns a word.
          A child who watches a parent give learns a habit.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <Divider />
      <h2 class="t-label faq-group">PRACTICAL</h2>

      <AccordionItem question="When and where does class meet?" id="faq-when">
        <p class="t-body">Sundays, from 10:00 AM until Salat al-Dhuhr, September through May.</p>
        <p class="t-body">
          Classes are held at the Islamic Education Center, 7917 Montrose Rd, Potomac, MD 20854.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question="Can I get involved?" id="faq-involved">
        <p class="t-body">Parent feedback and volunteering is encouraged.</p>
        <p class="t-body">
          The school is run by the families in it. If you have an hour, a skill, or a strong
          opinion about how something should be done, the school would rather hear it than not.
          Write to info@ispmd.org.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question="Is my donation tax-deductible?" id="faq-tax">
        <p class="t-body">
          Yes. The Islamic School of Potomac is a 501(c)(3) non-profit organization, EIN
          52-1989063. You can give through PayPal or by check.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>

      <AccordionItem question="How do I reach the school?" id="faq-reach">
        <p class="t-body">
          By phone at {site.phone.display}, or by email at {site.email.display}.
        </p>
      </AccordionItem>
    </Accordion>
  </Section>

  {/* 3. Aside */}
  <Section ground="warm" grid>
    <blockquote class="aside__quote">
      <p class="t-title t-italic" data-motion="line-rise">
        We are more than a Sunday School. We are a community.
      </p>
    </blockquote>

    <div class="aside__media">
      <Media slotId="faqs.aside" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 33vw, 90vw" />
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* 4. Still asking */}
  <Section ground="paper">
    <div class="still">
      <h2 class="t-display" data-motion="line-rise">Still asking?</h2>
      <p class="t-body" data-motion="body-rise">
        Write to info@ispmd.org. Ask anything.
      </p>
      <div class="still__actions" data-motion="body-rise">
        <Button href={site.email.href} variant="ghost">{site.email.display}</Button>
        <Button href="/contact" variant="quiet" icon="arrow-right">{labels.contact}</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ---- 2. The list ---- */

  .faq-group {
    padding-block: var(--s-5) var(--s-2);
  }

  .faq-group:first-child {
    padding-block-start: 0;
  }

  /* ---- 3. Aside ---- */

  .aside__quote,
  .aside__media {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .aside__quote { grid-column: 1 / 7; }
    .aside__media { grid-column: 7 / 11; }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .aside__quote { grid-column: 2 / 6; }
    .aside__media { grid-column: 7 / 11; }
  }

  /* ---- 4. Still asking ---- */

  .still {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-5);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .still__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--s-5) var(--s-7);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-2);
  }
</style>
